      <item>
        <title>AlphaProteo v3: 31% first-try binder success rate with conformer-aware design</title>
        <link>https://deepmind.com/alphaproteo-v3</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://deepmind.com/alphaproteo-v3</guid>
        <pubDate>Thu, 10 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>DeepMind blog</source>
        <description>AlphaProteo v3 is DeepMind&#x27;s de novo protein binder design model. The v3 release adds a conformer-aware diffusion head that conditions on the target&#x27;s bound-state conformation (not just the apo structure), lifting first-try success rate from 18% (v2) to 31%. On 12 therapeutic targets (PD-1, HER2, EGFRvIII, TNFα, IL-6R, VEGF, c-Met, BCL-2, KRAS-G12C, p53-R175H, Ras, β-amyloid), v3 designs binders with Kd &lt; 10 nM on 9/12 targets. Cryo-EM verifies the design matches the binding pose in 78% of cases (v2 was 71%). Released as open weights on HuggingFace under CC-BY-NC 4.0. The 8,400-binder library from v3 is downloadable as PDB + paired Kd + cryo-EM structures.</description>
        <category>Biology - De novo protein design</category>
        <dc:creator>DeepMind Isomorphic Sciences</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>BioNeMo-3: 12B-param drug discovery FM with diffusion-based pose refinement</title>
        <link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/bionemo-3</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/bionemo-3</guid>
        <pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>NVIDIA blog</source>
        <description>BioNeMo-3 (12B params) is NVIDIA&#x27;s third-generation drug-discovery foundation model, released at SC26. Trained on 3.2B protein sequences + 940M structures + 180M ligand-binding pairs. Key upgrade: a diffusion-based pose refinement head (DockingFuser v2) that iteratively refines binding poses. CASP17 GDT_TS 0.91 (beats AlphaFold 3&#x27;s 0.87 and ESM-4&#x27;s 0.92 by combining both architectures). DockingFuser v2 achieves 0.95 Top-1 pose accuracy on PDBbind-2026 (vs 0.92 in v1). Available via NIM containers + NGC catalog. Free academic access; commercial via NVIDIA AI Enterprise. Includes a 10,000-GPU academic credit programme.</description>
        <category>Biology - Drug discovery FM</category>
        <dc:creator>NVIDIA BioNeMo team</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>AlphaGenome 2: whole-genome variant effect prediction at 1Mbp context</title>
        <link>https://deepmind.com/alphagenome-2</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://deepmind.com/alphagenome-2</guid>
        <pubDate>Thu, 03 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>DeepMind blog</source>
        <description>AlphaGenome 2 is DeepMind&#x27;s foundation model for predicting the effects of genetic variants across the entire genome. The v2 release extends the context window from 100kbp to 1Mbp — long enough to capture enhancer-promoter loops and topologically-associating domains (TADs). On the Enformer-2026 benchmark (variant effect prediction for 35 tissues), AlphaGenome 2 achieves Pearson r=0.81 (vs r=0.61 for Enformer 2021, r=0.71 for Borzoi 2024). The 1Mbp context matters most for distal enhancers (&gt;100kbp from promoter), where AlphaGenome 2&#x27;s lead over Enformer grows to 0.21 r-units. Released as open weights (CC-BY-NC 4.0). Includes a unified API: given a VCF file, output predicted expression changes per tissue per variant.</description>
        <category>Genomics - Variant effect prediction</category>
        <dc:creator>DeepMind Genomics</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Mistral Med-Large: open-weight 70B medical LLM (Apache 2.0)</title>
        <link>https://mistral.ai/med-large</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mistral.ai/med-large</guid>
        <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Mistral AI blog</source>
        <description>Mistral Med-Large is a 70B-parameter medical LLM fine-tuned from Mistral Large 3 on 14M de-identified clinical notes + 6M PubMed abstracts + 2M medical exam Q&amp;A (USMLE + MRCP + PLAB). It is the first fully open-weight medical LLM at this scale. On the MedQA-USMLE benchmark, Mistral Med-Large achieves 89% (matching AMIE&#x27;s 85%, beating GPT-4o&#x27;s 73%). On the MultiMedQA suite (MedQA + PubMedQA + MedMCQA + MMLU-clinical), it scores 0.84 — beating the previous open-weight best (Meditron-3 70B) by 8 percentage points. Released under Apache 2.0 — the first 70B medical LLM fully available for commercial use. Includes a 5-shot prompting protocol + RAG template for clinical guidelines.</description>
        <category>CS - Medical LLM</category>
        <dc:creator>Mistral AI + Hugging Face</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Sora-vision medical: video-input multimodal LLM for clinical video review</title>
        <link>https://openai.com/sora-vision-medical</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://openai.com/sora-vision-medical</guid>
        <pubDate>Tue, 15 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>OpenAI technical report</source>
        <description>Sora-vision medical is OpenAI&#x27;s multimodal LLM fine-tuned from Sora 2 for clinical video review. Inputs: endoscopy video, surgical video, echocardiogram loops, ultrasound sweeps. Outputs: timestamped findings, severity grading, recommended next steps. On the OpenEndo-2026 benchmark (200 endoscopy videos × 5 findings each), Sora-vision medical achieves 0.87 mean average precision (mAP) — beating specialist models (Med-Gemini-Vid 0.74, General Sora 2 0.58). Mean time-to-first-finding: 4.2 seconds (vs 12.5s for a human endoscopist). Stanford GI pilot (3-month, 4 clinics): flagged 23 polyps that the endoscopist missed in real-time (24% of total polyps found) — likely representing the difference between early-stage detection and progression to cancer.</description>
        <category>CS - Medical video LLM</category>
        <dc:creator>OpenAI Health Sciences</dc:creator>
      </item>
